6. Practice 6: Using a political cartoon from the era related to “Choosing a Researchable Question,” (1) source it (who/when/purpose), (2) state one claim the document supports, (3) name one limitation or bias, (4) connect to a larger Unit 10 development in 3–5 sentences.

### Answer key (quality bar)

1. Sourcing is specific; claim is evidenced; limitation is honest; connection names causes/effects or continuity/change — not a moral slogan alone.
